$0(){return A.iQ(this.a,"# Get Schwifty \u2014 a patch STITCHED from meta: words.\nname Get Schwifty\n#\n# Each `meta:` below defines one module as a sequence of other words; a trailing\n# `\\` carries the definition onto the next line, a plain newline ends it. The\n# \"score\" at the very bottom just names the modules in order \u2014 that is the whole\n# instrument. Tweak a module's body and every use of it changes.\n\n# clock: the groove \u2014 a MIDI sequence whose pitch and gate are fanned out so two\n# voices can share them.\nmeta: clock filter MidiSequencer seq \\\n  knob seq bpm 128.0 \\\n  knob seq division 4 \\\n  knob seq gate_length 0.5 \\\n  knob seq notes C2 . Eb2 C2 G2 . Bb2 C3 \\\n  filter Copy2Cv pitchfan \\\n  patch seq out_cv -> pitchfan in_cv \\\n  filter Copy2Cv gatefan \\\n  patch seq out_gate -> gatefan in_cv\n\n# bass: a resonant saw plucked by an envelope \u2014 the acid bed. Takes its pitch\n# from pitchfan and its gate from gatefan (both minted by clock).\nmeta: bass filter ClassicOscillator vco \\\n  knob vco freq 440.0 \\\n  knob vco waveform 2 \\\n  patch pitchfan out_cv_a -> vco in_pitch_cv \\\n  filter ADSR env \\\n  knob env attack 0.004 \\\n  knob env decay 0.16 \\\n  knob env sustain 0.25 \\\n  knob env release 0.12 \\\n  patch gatefan out_cv_a -> env in_gate \\\n  filter Copy2Cv envfan \\\n  patch env out_cv -> envfan in_cv \\\n  filter SVF vcf \\\n  knob vcf cutoff 240.0 \\\n  knob vcf resonance 0.82 \\\n  knob vcf mode 0 \\\n  patch envfan out_cv_a -> vcf in_cutoff_cv \\\n  filter Volume bvca \\\n  patch envfan out_cv_b -> bvca in_gain_cv \\\n  patch vco out_pcm -> vcf in_pcm \\\n  patch vcf out_pcm -> bvca in_pcm\n\n# blip: a bitcrushed square an octave up, snapped by its own short envelope on\n# the same gate \u2014 the burp.\nmeta: blip filter ClassicOscillator zap \\\n  knob zap freq 880.0 \\\n  knob zap waveform 1 \\\n  patch pitchfan out_cv_b -> zap in_pitch_cv \\\n  filter Bitcrusher burp \\\n  knob burp target_rate 5000.0 \\\n  knob burp bit_depth 4 \\\n  knob burp mix 0.85 \\\n  patch zap out_pcm -> burp in_pcm \\\n  filter ADSR zenv \\\n  knob zenv attack 0.002 \\\n  knob zenv decay 0.09 \\\n  knob zenv sustain 0.0 \\\n  knob zenv release 0.05 \\\n  patch gatefan out_cv_b -> zenv in_gate \\\n  filter Volume zvca \\\n  patch zenv out_cv -> zvca in_gain_cv \\\n  patch burp out_pcm -> zvca in_pcm\n\n# portal: a low ring-modulated hum, always on (no gate) \u2014 the dimensional bed.\nmeta: portal filter Timer555 pa \\\n  knob pa freq 55.0 \\\n  knob pa duty_cycle 0.5 \\\n  filter ClassicOscillator pb \\\n  knob pb freq 82.5 \\\n  knob pb waveform 0 \\\n  filter SyncRing warp \\\n  knob warp depth 0.7 \\\n  knob warp normalize 2 \\\n  patch pa out_pcm -> warp in_pcm_a_carrier \\\n  patch pb out_pcm -> warp in_pcm_b_modulator \\\n  filter LowPass pfog \\\n  knob pfog cutoff 600.0 \\\n  patch warp out_pcm -> pfog in_pcm \\\n  filter Volume pvol \\\n  knob pvol volume 0.5 \\\n  patch pfog out_pcm -> pvol in_pcm\n\n# mix: wed the three voices, smear with a tape echo, then sum through a master\n# mixer whose second channel (in_pcm_b) is left FREE for a pedal lead \u2014 all held\n# under a limiter so the groove + lead can't clip.\nmeta: mix filter Mix2Pcm voices \\\n  knob voices normalize false \\\n  patch bvca out_pcm -> voices in_pcm_a \\\n  patch zvca out_pcm -> voices in_pcm_b \\\n  filter Mix2Pcm bed \\\n  knob bed normalize false \\\n  patch voices out_pcm -> bed in_pcm_a \\\n  patch pvol out_pcm -> bed in_pcm_b \\\n  filter Delay echo \\\n  knob echo time 0.28 \\\n  knob echo feedback 0.4 \\\n  knob echo mix 0.3 \\\n  patch bed out_pcm -> echo in_pcm \\\n  filter Mix2Pcm master \\\n  knob master normalize false \\\n  patch echo out_pcm -> master in_pcm_a \\\n  filter Limiter lim \\\n  knob lim ceiling 0.9 \\\n  patch master out_pcm -> lim in_pcm \\\n  output lim out_pcm\n\n# --- The score: name the modules in order and the instrument assembles itself.\nclock\nbass\nblip\nportal\nmix\n\n# --- The Schwifty pedal: one free-hanging control, bolted on after the score \u2014\n# no meta:, just plain commands reaching into what the words already built. Hold\n# it (Gate) to sing a saw lead over the groove, into the master mixer's free\n# channel that `mix` left open. The portal hum stays on underneath as the bed. ---\nfilter ClassicOscillator lead\nknob lead freq 523.25\nknob lead waveform 2\nfilter LowPass leadlp\nknob leadlp cutoff 3200.0\npatch lead out_pcm -> leadlp in_pcm\nfilter Volume leadvca\nknob leadvca volume 0.8\npatch leadlp out_pcm -> leadvca in_pcm\nfilter Pedal schwifty\nknob schwifty mode 0\nknob schwifty time 0.3\npatch schwifty out_cv -> leadvca in_gain_cv\npatch leadvca out_pcm -> master in_pcm_b\n\npanel knob schwifty pedal\npanel knob schwifty mode\npanel knob vcf cutoff\npanel knob vcf resonance\npanel knob seq bpm\n\n"+A.ho())},
